        "input": {
          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory course audience.",
          "text": "A frequency-response plot puts driving frequency on the horizontal axis and response amplitude on the vertical axis. The peak marks the resonant region. Its location and width tell engineers which excitations are most dangerous or most useful. A design does not merely ask whether a force exists; it asks how often that force repeats."
