        "input": {
          "instructions": "Professional, concise, and paced for an introductory course audience.",
          "text": "Every oscillating mechanical system has ways it naturally prefers to move. Push a swing slowly, or far too quickly, and the motion stays modest. Push near its natural rhythm and each input can reinforce the motion already underway. That frequency-sensitive amplification is the core idea behind resonance."
